# The XNU patch directory the format 1 build globs is composed, not tracked: it is UniXNU's
# shared series plus this board's patches from patches/xnu-device/. Committing it would make the
# shared half drift silently whenever UniXNU updates a patch, and a device repository's own
# patches/xnu/ *replaces* UniXNU's rather than adding to it (see 3.29). scripts/compose-xnu-patches.py
# writes it; every build path, local and CI, runs that first.
/patches/xnu/

# Build outputs and caches (re-derivable; nothing important lives here)
/build/
/Build/
/Conf/
/out/
/.cache/
/refer/
/.local*/
/Mu_Basecore/
# The repository's own work/ tree: host test objects, probe executables and the
# 32 MiB pulled log windows. Anchored to the repository root on purpose - there is
# an UNRELATED work/ directory one level up in the port working directory, outside
# this repository, and a bare `work/` or `**/work/` rule would be ambiguous about
# which one is meant. Nothing under this work/ was ever tracked (git ls-files
# work/ = 0), so ignoring it changes no existing file; it exists because an
# unqualified `git add -A` DID stage the whole tree once and had to be unstaged.
/work/

# What scripts/dump-device-facts.sh writes. It is this phone's own dump and does not belong to the
# repository: the values it produces are copied into board.toml by hand, on purpose.
/enchilada-facts/
/backup/

# Local development files
*.log
*.terminal
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.dSYM/

# Inputs, images and products that never belong in Git
*.ipsw
*.dmg
*.im4p
*.img
*.dbr
*.macho
*.o
*.a
*.dylib
*.efi
*.dtb
*.bc
*.spv
*.metallib
*.bin
*.mbn
*.fw
*.pem
*.key
.env
local.toml

# The A630 firmware blobs pulled read-only from this phone's own vendor_a partition.
# scripts/data/adreno-a630-device-firmware.json records their SIZES + HASHES + PIL
# structure as durable text, on purpose: the proprietary BYTES are somebody else's
# signed firmware and must never enter this repository. The extraction writes them to
# work/tmp/a630-device-fw/, which on the current host sits OUTSIDE this worktree, so
# nothing there is committable today; the rules below are the belt for the case where
# someone later copies the directory in. *.mdt and *.b0N are stated explicitly because
# neither had any rule before ROUND 107: only the .bin and .fw suffixes were covered,
# so 5 of the 7 blobs were committable the moment they landed inside the worktree.
# NOT covered on purpose: *.elf. The suffix is far too common among ordinary build
# products to ignore repo-wide, and the directory rule already catches the one .elf
# that belongs to this firmware set.
/work/tmp/a630-device-fw/
*.mdt
*.b0[0-9]
